  "details": "1. Open VRChat\n\n2. Open your large VRC Menu\n\n3. [REQUIREMENT: 200, 500, 700 or 100 notifications, in this case, friend requests]\n\n4. Click the \"Notifications\" tab.\n\n5. Your game should buffer, proportionally to the amount of notifiactions and the time it takes for each notifiaction to load into memory. Time can vary:\n\nPC: \n\n200 Notifs - ~1 seconds freeze\n\n500 notifs - ~2 seconds freeze\n\n700 notifs - ~5 seconds freeze\n\n1000 notifs - ~8 seconds freeze\n\n(Phone -, relative to each phone's processor.)\n\nProposed solution would be buffering notifications in packets of 50's instead of all 700 or 1000 at once. I cannot count the amount of times I've ended up accidentally pressing the notification tab, greeted with the 'great freeze.'\n\nHere is a clip on android phone of the \"great freeze,\" I was currently standing at 730 notifiactions:",
